      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-09-23_WidnesExaminer_art0034" n="art0034">
        <head>SORE HEADS AT SCHOOL.</head>
        <p>SORE HEADS AT SCHOOL.</p>
        <p>1 Zam-Buk Stops Epidemic and Eradicates Disease.</p>
        <p>1 No skin complaints are more common among school children than diseases of the scalp, and they spread so easily from one child to another that mothers need to be ever watchful. Zam-Buk not only cures individual cases, however obstinate, but by preventing infection stamps out epidemics. Mrs. James, Bentley, the wife of an insurance agent, of 29, Gibson-street, Commercial-road, Halifax, said to a "Halifax Guardian " reporter :—" About Christmas time a very bad ringworm appeared on my Sidney's temple. He was examined at school by a doctor, who said these cases were very common, and sent him home at once to prevent the disease spreading to the other scholars. At any infirmary he remained an out-patient for three months, and the doctors supplied me with 'paint' to put on the ringworm. As soon as I applied it, however, the affected part became covered with a ' mass of scabs, at least half an inch in thickness, I am the mother of five, but I have never seen anything like this boy's bead was at that time. Ho seemed very poor in health, too, and at nights had to lie on his forehead to get ease. No one but myself would look at the boy's bead—it was so disagreeable in appearance. His hair came off on one side of the head. I "I used linseed poultices withoufavail, and was ready to despair. At last I resorted to Zam-Buk, and within two days the smaller scabs began to rise at the edges from the skin. I stopped taking the boy to the Infirmary, and set myself to give Zam-Buk a fair chance,6l I was concerned lest my other children caught the I disease too, and I was extremely carefnl to keep clean 1 the cloths used. Altogether I used three boxes, of I Zam-Buk, and Sidney's head was completely cured in 1 three weeks. His head is perfectly clear of the disease 1 and ho is wonderfully well too." 1 Zam-Buk is antiseptic as well as healing, and it kills off microbes and parasites, thus preventing the spread of disease and stamp 1 s it out completely. Zarn-Buk permanently cures all scalp diseases, scabs, ringworm, running sores, honey sickness, the effects of dandruff and scurvy, eczema, psoriasis, sore backs, abscesses boils, pimples, chafing, sore faces, chapped hands chills, festering sores, poisoned wounds, piles, stiffness 1 aching feet, sprains, cuts, bruises, rheumatism and t nerve pains. Of all chemists, or the Zam-Buk Co., 4, I Red Cross-street, London, E.G., for Is. L'Al. or 23. 9d. perfbox (2s. 9d. size contains nearly -four times the Ts. Id.) Every home needs it!</p>
